{
    "background_story": "Cherub, a gentle angel, was tasked with watching over the mortal realm. As he gazed down upon the humans, he noticed a peculiar affliction affecting many of their eyes - a pinguecula, a growth on the conjunctiva that seemed to bring discomfort and blurred vision. Moved by their struggles, Cherub descended to the mortal realm to offer his assistance. With a touch of his divine hand, he soothed the irritated eyes, calming the inflammation and restoring clarity to their sight. As news of his healing spread, people began to call upon Cherub for relief from this pesky condition. And so, the angel continued to watch over humanity, ever vigilant and ready to lend his aid to those afflicted by pinguecula and other eye troubles.",
